<title>USA: TABLE - Imperial Q2 oper shr $0.35 vs $0.18.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Imperial Q2 oper shr $0.35 vs $0.18.</headline>
<dateline>TORRANCE, Calif. 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second quarter ended June 30</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Oper Shr		   $0.35		    $0.18</p>
<p> Shr			   0.35		     1.11</p>
<p> Net			   14.1		     43.0</p>
<p> Revs			  57.5		     96.1</p>
<p> Avg shrs		    40.8		     38.8</p>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.55		    $0.36</p>
<p> Shr			   0.52		     1.39</p>
<p> Net			   21.1		     51.7</p>
<p> Revs			  97.8		    140.4</p>
<p> Avg			   40.8		     37.2</p>
<p>(All data above in millions except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: The company's full name is Imperial Credit Industries Inc. The 1996 net results include a $62.0 million gain from selling 42 percent of its stake in Southern Pacific Funding Corp in June 1996.</p>
<p>The 1997 net results include a $4.3 million gain from selling an additional two percent of its stake in Southern and a $4.0 million charge from retiring debt.</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding are fully-diluted.</p>
